{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_13-42-19-etcd_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nu={\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Interpret the retained CheckQuorum execution (CheckRun 8090da09e0d44e13af56696a62f13d45, fixed experiment bbdf8837c719466ba9f5044f34c9c29f-experiment, version 4): seventeen parsed events without loss, the two earlier scenarios repeat their outcomes, and the new scenario shows the stale answer is not removed by CheckQuorum but is bounded by the step-down one heartbeat interval later. The question record's discriminator is narrowed to the routes that remain unmeasured.\\\",\n \\\"investigations\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"9ad1a10e85bb41578fbb8a42a6890ab3-question-0\\\",\n  \\\"discriminator\\\":\\\"Whether the same missing membership check produces a stale answer through a route that was not exercised - a forwarded MsgReadIndex answered with MsgReadIndexResp, or a lease-based read configuration - and whether PreVote combined with CheckQuorum changes the measured one-heartbeat bound.\\\"}],\n \\\"interpretations\\\":[{\n  \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"9ad1a10e85bb41578fbb8a42a6890ab3-question-0\\\",\n  \\\"experiment_id\\\":\\\"bbdf8837c719466ba9f5044f34c9c29f-experiment\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"tracker-singleton\\\",\\\"readindex-singleton-branch\\\",\\\"prop-removed-leader\\\",\\\"switchtoconfig-removal\\\",\\\"config-stepdown-doc\\\",\\\"readonlysafe-doc\\\",\\\"node-readindex-contract\\\",\\\"readme-linearizable\\\"],\n  \\\"executions\\\":{\\\"8090da09e0d44e13af56696a62f13d45\\\":[12,13,14,15,16]},\n  \\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"violated\\\",\n  \\\"defect_claim\\\":\\\"asserted\\\",\n  \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The question's account is now complete in three measured shapes and one measured bound. Root cause (source side): the ReadIndex path never asks whether the local node belongs to its own configuration - tracker.IsSingleton (tracker/tracker.go:158-162) is a size test whose comment asserts that the single voting member is the leader, stepLeader's MsgReadIndex case (raft.go:1354-1361) answers locally from r.raftLog.committed when the test holds (ReadState for a local request, MsgReadIndexResp for a forwarded one) and otherwise accepts the request into readOnly (raft.go:2160-2166), while the write path refuses proposals from exactly this node (raft.go:1294-1303); the state is produced by permitted use because applying a committed change that removes the leading node leaves it leading under the default Config.StepDownOnRemoval=false (raft.go:1985-2012, raft.go:282-287). Measured in receipt 8090da09e0d44e13af56696a62f13d45: single-voter remainder without the quorum check - the removed leader answers the read with index 2 while the actual leader has committed 4, sending no message at all (parsed index 3), the actual leader answers the same request with index 4 (index 4), and the removed leader repeats index 2 after three heartbeat intervals (index 5). Two-voter remainder - the same removal leaves singleton false while the node still leads, and the request is accepted into readOnly and never confirmed (index 9: read_answered false with a read context in the heartbeats, unconfirmed_reads 1) remaining so after three further intervals (index 10). Single-voter remainder with Config.CheckQuorum enabled - the removal still leaves singleton true and the stale answer is issued before the quorum check can do anything (index 14: read_states 1, read_index 2 against the actual leader's committed 4), and then the bound appears: the current leader answers the removed leader's old-term heartbeat with its higher term, so after one heartbeat tick the node is StateFollower at term 2 with no leader (index 15, ticks_until_stepdown 1), and a further request is not answered at all because the node has no leader (index 16, new_read_states 0). The account therefore states: on a node that its own configuration proves is not the voter, a client can be handed an index that misses entries the actual leader has already committed, with no confirmation round; when the remainder has more than one voter the same missing check yields an unanswerable request instead of a wrong answer; and the exposure is bounded by the configuration - with CheckQuorum the stale answer stops being available one heartbeat interval after the new leader is elected, when the removed leader steps down, and the request is then refused/dropped rather than answered from a stale state. The defect is not repaired inside raft: the request the node accepted is neither answered with a current index nor rejected with an error, and the client must retry elsewhere.\\\",\n  \\\"counterevidence\\\":[\n   \\\"The control comparison at parsed index 4 holds: the same request answered by the node that is the actual leader returns an index covering its commit index, so answering locally is not itself the defect - the violation depends on the answering node not being the configuration's voter.\\\",\n   \\\"The measured bound limits the impact: with CheckQuorum the removed leader steps down after one heartbeat tick (parsed index 15) and stops answering (index 16), so the stale answer is available only in the interval between the new leader's election and the next heartbeat exchange.\\\",\n   \\\"In the two-voter shape no wrong index is produced (parsed index 9: read_answered false), so that shape is a liveness symptom rather than a stale-read symptom, and the Node.ReadIndex contract already tells callers that read index requests can be lost and that retries are their duty (node.go:218-224); it is recorded as part of this mechanism, not as an independent safety claim.\\\",\n   \\\"A client is expected to direct linearizable reads at the current leader, and the library cannot generally detect that a leader is stale; what is specific here is that the local tracker already establishes that the only voter is another node, and that the same library refuses this node's proposals.\\\"\n  ],\n  \\\"limitations\\\":[\n   \\\"The scenario requires the application to apply a committed configuration change that removes the leading node while Config.StepDownOnRemoval is false; applications that set that option, or that stop the removed node, do not reach it.\\\",\n   \\\"The witness is at the ReadIndex contract level: the receipt shows the returned index is below an already-committed entry and that no confirmation message was sent. No state machine was run, so the miss of that write in a served value is a consequence of the contract, not something the receipt measures.\\\",\n   \\\"The measured bound is one heartbeat interval in the exercised configuration (one heartbeat tick, election timeout ten); the receipt does not measure other tick ratios, PreVote combined with CheckQuorum, or lease-based reads.\\\",\n   \\\"Only requests addressed to the removed node itself were exercised. The forwarded route (a follower's MsgReadIndex answered with MsgReadIndexResp) rests on the same branch, but in the single-voter shape such a follower would be the singleton voter itself and nothing newer would be committed at that moment, so no stale outcome was constructed for it.\\\"\n  ],\n  \\\"knowledge\\\":[\n   {\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"9ad1a10e85bb41578fbb8a42a6890ab3-knowledge-0\\\",\\\"revision\\\":1,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"IsSingleton is a size-only test over the configuration and never compares the single voter with the local node.\\\"},\n   {\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"9ad1a10e85bb41578fbb8a42a6890ab3-knowledge-1\\\",\\\"revision\\\":1,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"StepLeader answers MsgReadIndex locally whenever IsSingleton holds, using its own commit index and without a round.\\\"},\n   {\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"9ad1a10e85bb41578fbb8a42a6890ab3-knowledge-2\\\",\\\"revision\\\":1,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"A removed leader keeps leading by default while its proposals are refused and its read answers are not.\\\"}\n  ]}]}\nopen('update9.json','w').write(json.dumps(u,indent=2)+\\\"\\\\n\\\")\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_13-42-19-etcd_raft-real-run --submission update9.json 2>&1 | tail -5\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
